{
 "idea": {
  "id": "short_market",
  "family": "short-flow",
  "title": "Buy the index when off-exchange short volume across large stocks is unusually high",
  "why": "Added up across the largest stocks, the share of off-exchange volume marked short is a gauge of how much buying market makers absorbed that day (they sell short to fill buyers). SqueezeMetrics' dark-pool index is this number, and its claim is that high readings come before above-average index returns over the following days and weeks. The mirror test is that low readings come before weak ones.",
  "source": "SqueezeMetrics 2018 (DIX white paper)",
